{
  "notes": [
    "Shared offline subprocess conformance cases consumed by tests/test_subproc_lifecycle.py, ts/tests/subproc-lifecycle.test.ts (against ts/src) and ts/tests/node-lifecycle.mjs (against ts/dist).",
    "Each case runs in a fresh temporary directory. argv/cwd tokens: {python} = interpreter, {tests} = this directory, {dir} = the case directory. `files` are written into {dir} before launch (mode is a decimal POSIX mode).",
    "`options` use the TypeScript option names; Python maps them to snake_case. `stdin` may be a string, null, absent, or {repeat, times}. `onOutput: true` attaches a chunk collector, so runners that cannot stream (TypeScript sync) must be excluded. `cancel` is `beforeLaunch` (already cancelled) or `afterReady` (triggered once {dir}/ready exists). `gracefulSignal` selects the one signal sent to the group before SIGKILL escalation (default SIGTERM).",
    "`runners` lists the entry points per language; a case missing from a language, or listing an entry point that cannot honor its options, fails that language's coverage guard. Sync/async differences are stated in `note`.",
    "Duration bounds derive from the engine's cleanup budget (0.5s TERM grace + 1s drain = 1.5s) plus 1.5s of scheduling slack; `maxDurationSeconds` includes the run's own deadline and fixture startup. `stdoutLength`/`stderrLength` count decoded characters and are only used with ASCII content."
  ],
  "categories": ["spawn", "stdinEof", "signal", "timeout", "cancellation", "grandchildren", "flood", "chunkBoundary"],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "spawn-missing-executable",
      "category": "spawn",
      "argv": ["{dir}/no-such-binary"],
      "options": {"timeoutSeconds": 5},
      "runners": {"python": ["sync", "async"], "typescript": ["sync", "async"]},
      "expect": {
        "termination": "launch-failed",
        "launchError": "ENOENT",
        "exitCode": -1,
        "timedOut": false,
        "signal": null,
        "timeoutKind": null,
        "maxDurationSeconds": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "spawn-missing-cwd",
      "category": "spawn",
      "argv": ["sh", "-c", "true"],
      "cwd": "{dir}/gone",
      "options": {"timeoutSeconds": 5},
      "runners": {"python": ["sync", "async"], "typescript": ["sync", "async"]},
      "expect": {
        "termination": "launch-failed",
        "launchError": "ENOENT",
        "exitCode": -1,
        "timedOut": false,
        "signal": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "spawn-non-executable-file",
      "category": "spawn",
      "files": {"not-executable": {"content": "#!/bin/sh\necho ran\n", "mode": 384}},
      "argv": ["{dir}/not-executable"],
      "options": {"timeoutSeconds": 5},
      "runners": {"python": ["sync", "async"], "typescript": ["sync", "async"]},
      "expect": {
        "termination": "launch-failed",
        "launchError": "EACCES",
        "exitCode": -1,
        "timedOut": false,
        "signal": null,
        "stdout": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exit-nonzero-is-exited",
      "category": "spawn",
      "argv": ["sh", "-c", "exit 3"],
      "options": {"timeoutSeconds": 5},
      "runners": {"python": ["sync", "async"], "typescript": ["sync", "async"]},
      "expect": {
        "termination": "exited",
        "exitCode": 3,
        "timedOut": false,
        "signal": null,
        "launchError": null,
        "timeoutKind": null,
        "callbackError": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "stdin-absent-is-eof",
      "category": "stdinEof",
